  "body": "It does use [`FileSender`](https://twistedmatrix.com/documents/current/api/twisted.protocols.basic.FileSender.html), which reads the file in chunks and so shouldn't be *too* slow, but nonetheless there is potential for disk I/O to take a long time (especially with networked storage).\r\n\r\nWe should look into either a) doing async file I/O (though that is likely hard) or b) do the reads from a thread.",
